ot/issues/comments/6133785834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124328#issuecomment-6133785834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124328","id":6133785834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbZok6g","user":{"login":"ajreckof","id":66184050,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MTg0MDUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66184050?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof","html_url":"https://github.com/ajreckof","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ajreckof/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T22:27:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T22:27:08Z","body":"Ok I did not know there was this other problem and as is my fix did not fix this case as i did not think about what happens when there is not enough min space to fit it centered. I've slightly updated my solution but as is this does not keep the tabbar centered but push it away from the center to repect both its minimum size and the minimum size of things around it.\r\n\r\nI think aven if we go with my pr instead of yours. Your PR would still be usefull in case we want to keep it centered as much as possible or anyway in case both side have things that make the whole bar full and we want to reduce the overall minimum size. \r\n\r\n\r\nWhile testing for this I have found that Tab Bar desired size did not account well for hav